This role will report directly to the AVP of Engineering and will be responsible for bringing new innovation in QA Processes and building frameworks from scratch to ensure a successful bug-free software release to production.

Role And Responsibilities

You will be responsible for Defining QA strategy, approach, and execution in development projects.
The role requires strategic thinking and planning and provide leadership and technical expertise within Test Automation and Quality Assurance throughout the entire product development life cycle with a strong sense of quality ownership making sure that quality is baked in from the start.
Your primary focus will be to achieve quality through Automation
The Head of QA will have ownership of QA environments across Multiple products and will work closely with the DevOps team to define the optimal solution for each platform.
As the Head of QA you will oversee the delivery and maintenance of automated scenarios and frameworks based on industry best practice and will be responsible for leading and directing the QA leadership team.
You will be responsible for Leading and directing the QA leadership team a large team of QC professionals spanning across Product Lines.
Provide technical leadership and expertise within the field of Automation Testing, to continuously enhance the framework.
Ensuring that the development teams adhere to the principles, guidelines and best practices of the QA strategy as defined Focus on continuous QA improvements including usage of appropriate testing tools, test techniques, test automation.
Building and maintenance of quality standards as well as enforcing technical and testing standards
Automation expertise –
Increase Test coverage, improve and automate Test strategies and software configurations during system testing.
Implement and develop Test automation framework which fulfils the diverse needs of complex products and is the sole certification criteria for Product releases.
Responsible for the creation, execution and maintenance of automated scripts, tracking/reporting results, troubleshooting and coordinating defect resolution, in an automated fashion.
Guide the teams to Develop concise and easy to maintain test scripts that can be reused across a sub-system or feature.
Develop and maintain load & performance testing/ create metrics as and when required.

Job Description

Overall 14+ years of experience in defining QA strategy, approach and execution in development projects
The individual must have a proven track record of building QA teams, managing the function and direction of the QA teams.
Experience in executing load and performance testing; ability to find application weaknesses.

Five Reasons Why You Should Join Zycus

Cloud Product Company: We are a Cloud SaaS Company and our products are created by using the latest technologies like ML and AI. Our UI is in Angular JS and we are developing our mobile apps using React.
A Market Leader: Zycus is recognized by Gartner (world’s leading market research analyst) as a Leader in Procurement Software Suites.
Move between Roles: We believe that change leads to growth and therefore we allow our employees to shift careers and move to different roles and functions within the organization
Get a Global Exposure: You get to work and deal with our global customers.
Create an Impact: Zycus gives you the environment to create an impact on the product and transform your ideas into reality. Even our junior engineers get the opportunity to work on different product features.